  "pseudos": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In a classic case of the house always winning, the Vegas Golden Knights completed a four-game Western Conference Final sweep, sending the Colorado Avalanche packing. The desert gladiators, led by the emergency button that was coach John Tortorella, slammed the door shut in Game 4 with a 2-1 victory, sealing Colorado's season with a whimper after their stars aligned for the infirmary, sidelining key talents Cale Makar and Nathan MacKinnon.",
